0</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134684452,imgsize-92396.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Justice Bhuyan's remarks prove CEC violated Constitution: Congress]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/justice-bhuyans-remarks-prove-cec-violated-constitution-congress/articleshow/134683628.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134683628.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress General Secretary Jairam Ramesh stated that Justice Ujjal Bhuyan affirmed the right to vote's significance in the Constitution. He emphasized that this opinion indicates a violation by Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. Ramesh argued that Bhuyan's remarks undermine Kumar's position as a constitutional authority. Additionally, he suggested that Kumar should resign due to losing his moral authority.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/justice-bhuyans-remarks-prove-cec-violated-constitution-congress/articleshow/134683628.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/justice-bhuyans-remarks-prove-cec-violated-constitution-congress/articleshow/134683628.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T07:09:30+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134683638,imgsize-52636.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Democracy in peril as voters illegally ousted: Former SC judge Justice Rohinton Fali Nariman]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/democracy-in-peril-as-voters-illegally-ousted-former-sc-judge-justice-rohinton-fali-nariman/articleshow/134680618.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134680618.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Justice Rohinton Fali Nariman expressed concerns regarding the functioning of the Election Commission in India. He highlighted the issue of illegal removal of voters from electoral lists, especially in West Bengal. Nariman noted that 90 lakh voters were disenfranchised, with many not having access to justice. He emphasized the need for reform in the appointment process of election commissioners to ensure fairness.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/democracy-in-peril-as-voters-illegally-ousted-former-sc-judge-justice-rohinton-fali-nariman/articleshow/134680618.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/democracy-in-peril-as-voters-illegally-ousted-former-sc-judge-justice-rohinton-fali-nariman/articleshow/134680618.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T03:34:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amit Anand Choudhary</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134680631,imgsize-52346.cms"/></item></channel></rss>